codex
The tree uses several policies: silent storage, silent no-ops, bounded diagnostics, repeated diagnostics, masking, and device error responses. I also found a relevant counterexample: SH4’s RCR1 arm declines unsupported writes, and its comment explicitly discusses the former store-before-exit ordering. For LCA, both status registers still fall through to the terminating default; the header marks two bits in STAT0 as write-one-to-clear.

