1717:
1718:/*
1719: *  #447: four value guards in the switch below ended the host process with exit(1) on
1720: *  ONE ordinary guest store -- TCR, DMATCR, ICR and RCR1.  MEASURED on an unmodified
1721: *  -E landisk, each with a matched surviving control at the SAME address and the SAME
1722: *  width, so it is the VALUE that kills and not the address or the access width.
1723: *
1724: *  Fixed in the #438/#441/#443 shape -- keep the diagnostic, drop the exit(1), ignore
1725: *  the write -- and the four arms differ in a way that is invisible at the call site:
1726: *
1727: *    RCR1    the store was UPSTREAM of the guard.  Dropping exit(1) alone would have
1728: *            turned a host kill into SILENT STATE CORRUPTION.  Moved below the guard.
1729: *    TCR     `timer_hz` was set from `idata & 3` BEFORE the guard and the debug() line
1730: *            had already announced it, so the naive fix installs a timer frequency the
1731: *            guest never asked for.  The guard moved ABOVE the prescaler switch.
1732: *    DMATCR  the store is already downstream; nothing to move.
1733: *    ICR     nothing is stored on any path, so there is no state to corrupt.
